  <entry>
    <id>http://arxiv.org/abs/2401.00120v1</id>
    <title>Eigenstates in the self-organised criticality</title>
    <updated>2023-12-30T02:34:02Z</updated>
    <link href="https://arxiv.org/abs/2401.00120v1" rel="alternate" type="text/html"/>
    <link href="https://arxiv.org/pdf/2401.00120v1" rel="related" type="application/pdf" title="pdf"/>
    <summary>We employ the eigen microstate approach to explore the self-organized criticality (SOC) in two celebrated sandpile models, namely, the BTW model and the Manna model. In both models, phase transitions from the absorbing-state to the critical state can be understood by the emergence of dominant eigen microstates with significantly increased weights. Spatial eigen microstates of avalanches can be uniformly characterized by a linear system size rescaling. The first temporal eigen microstates reveal scaling relations in both models. Furthermore, by finite-size scaling analysis of the first eigen microstate, we numerically estimate critical exponents i.e., $\sqrt{σ_0 w_1}/\tilde{v}_{1} \propto L^D$ and $\tilde{v}_{1} \propto L^{D(1-τ_s)/2}$. Our findings could provide profound insights into eigen states of the universality and phase transition in non-equilibrium complex systems governed by self-organized criticality.</summary>
    <category term="physics.soc-ph" scheme="http://arxiv.org/schemas/atom"/>
    <category term="cond-mat.stat-mech" scheme="http://arxiv.org/schemas/atom"/>
