    <id>http://arxiv.org/abs/2212.14726v3</id>
    <title>$1/\varphi$ Spectrum of the Stress Dynamics with the Bak-Tang-Wiesenfeld Sandpile</title>
    <updated>2024-03-23T15:12:25Z</updated>
    <link href="https://arxiv.org/abs/2212.14726v3" rel="alternate" type="text/html"/>
    <link href="https://arxiv.org/pdf/2212.14726v3" rel="related" type="application/pdf" title="pdf"/>
    <summary>With the original Bak-Tang-Wisenefeld (BTW) sandpile we uncover the $1/\varphi$ noise in the mechanism maintaining self-organized criticality (SOC) - the question raised together with the concept of SOC. We posit that the dynamics of stress in the BTW sandpile follows quasi-cycles of graduate stress accumulation that end up with an abrupt stress-release and the drop of the system to subcritical state. In thermodynamic limit, the intra-cycle dynamics exhibits the $1/\varphi$ spectrum that extends infinitely and corresponds to the stress-release within the critical state.</summary>
